      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "On a peak of San Cha Mountain, Tie Ruo Nan clears nearly a thousand ash-grey mountain apes with golden needle Gu pairings, then climbs to Tie Mu Bai. He praises her grasp of those tactics and shows a finer cloud of golden needle Gu that moves like golden fog with create fog Gu, perforating boulders and nearby trees. He names Luchuan River for that fog at age twenty-eight while roaming Southern Border, then names Tie Mu mountain as the place he reached at age forty-two after advancing to rank four peak stage and leaving closed cultivation to test his skills, where more than fifty demonic path mountain bandits attacked him.",
      "chapters": [
        374
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
